%description:

Tcp.fastopenCookieCacheSize:invalid -- a cache of 0 entries stops the run with an error.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "at least 1".

The classes: ample (1024, the default: more servers than the test uses), evicts (a value below
the number of servers: a new server replaces an entry), invalid (below 1). The code:
Tcp::setFastOpenCookie() removes an arbitrary entry when the cache is full; Tcp::initialize()
checks the value.

Host under test: host1. Observation: the error, and the exit code of the run.

%# parameter: Tcp.fastopenCookieCacheSize
%# class: invalid
%# value: 0
%# key: *.host1.tcp.fastopenCookieCacheSize
%# expected-result: PASS

%activity:
EV << "TcpFastopenCookieCacheSizeInvalid compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.fastopenCookieCacheSize = 0    # the parameter under test
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%exitcode: 1

%contains-regex: stderr
fastopenCookieCacheSize must be 1 or more, but it is 0
